<title>NETHERLANDS: Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</title>
<headline>Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp product stock levels.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oil product inventories held in independent tankage in the Amsterdam-Rotterdam-Antwerp area were estimated to be at the following levels currently, a week ago and a year ago, industry sources said.</p>
<p>All figures in thousands of tonnes:</p>
<p>		     21/11/96		 14/11/96	    24/11/95</p>
<p>    Gasoline	    450			450		   375</p>
<p>    Naphtha	  75-100		   75-100		75-100</p>
<p>    Gas oil	   2,100		    1,950		 1,900</p>
<p>    Fuel oil	    375		  375-400		   500</p>
<p>    Jet kero	     25			 25		 10-15</p>
<p>Gas oil stocks rose with the contining arrival of cargoes from the U.S. and the CIS and some shifting of product from refineries to storage within ARA, all done in readiness for the record IPE delivery. Subsequent movements have been hampered by the lack of barge avails.</p>
<p>Gasoline stocks were steady, although some cargoes left for the UK. Naphtha inventories were flat, movement was slight.</p>
<p>Fuel oil inventories dipped as no cargoes arrived, but product left for the bunker market.</p>
<p>A cargo of jet arrived, but went swiftly to the gas oil pool for blending.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom, +31 20 504 5004</p>
</text>
